    "result_text": "All 32 tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n- Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- After a successful `saveOwner`, it emits an audit line carrying the newly assigned owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n  ```\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the success path (after all validation and after the id is assigned by save), so the `id`, `customerCode`, and business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` all match the persisted/echoed-back values that `Cp21Tests` asserts against. The new test `Cp21Tests` passes and the full suite (32 tests) is green.",
